From: =?UTF-8?q?J=C3=A1nos=20Mik=C3=B3?=
 <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 17:29:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 025/154] fix: guard the two null-service derefs that crash the
 context menu
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Right-clicking selected text segfaulted the BROWSER process, taking the whole
session with it. Stack in build/logs/crash-context-menu-2026-08-06.log:

    Received signal 11 SEGV_ACCERR 000000000018
    RenderViewContextMenu::AppendSearchProvider() + 352
    RenderViewContextMenu::AppendRevisedTextSelectionSection() + 148
    RenderViewContextMenu::InitMenu() + 840

AppendSearchProvider dereferences two profile-keyed services without checking
either:

    AutocompleteClassifierFactory::GetForProfile(GetProfile())->Classify(...)
    TemplateURLServiceFactory::GetForProfile(GetProfile())->GetDefaultSearchProvider()

Both return null for a profile their factory does not serve. Address 0x18 is a
member access on null, and everything above the first call early-returns, which
is why it only fires with a non-empty selection - right-clicking with nothing
selected never reaches it.

Upstream can assume every tab-hosting profile has these, because it only hosts
tabs on profiles ProfileManager built for that purpose. Atrium creates one per
space and hands them to windows directly, so the assumption does not hold.

Degrading to "no Search-the-web item" is the right failure: the menu stays
usable and nothing else in it depends on either service. Note the null RESULT
of GetDefaultSearchProvider was already handled upstream - only the null
SERVICE was not.

MITIGATION, not a root cause. Which profile returns null, and why, is still
open: profiles come from ProfileManager::GetProfileByPath, and a regular
profile should get both services. The crash is worth stopping first - it
destroys a browsing session - but the cause stays open.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../render_view_context_menu.cc               | 35 ++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/renderer_context_menu/render_view_context_menu.cc b/chrome/browser/renderer_context_menu/render_view_context_menu.cc
index b4a0392ee870e..d6e2c8870fb88 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/renderer_context_menu/render_view_context_menu.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/renderer_context_menu/render_view_context_menu.cc
@@ -2876,10 +2876,29 @@ void RenderViewContextMenu::AppendSearchProvider() {
   base::ReplaceChars(params_.selection_text, AutocompleteInput::kInvalidChars,
                      u" ", &params_.selection_text);
 
+  // ATRIUM: both service lookups in this function are dereferenced
+  // unguarded upstream, and either returns null for a profile its factory does
+  // not serve. Right-clicking selected text then segfaults the BROWSER process
+  // and takes the whole session with it - reported on a five-profile setup,
+  // with the crash at this line (SEGV_ACCERR on a null + 0x18).
+  //
+  // Upstream can assume every tab-hosting profile has these because it only
+  // ever hosts tabs on profiles ProfileManager built for that purpose. Atrium
+  // creates one per space and hands them to windows directly, so the
+  // assumption does not hold here.
+  //
+  // Degrading to "no Search-the-web item" is the correct failure: the menu is
+  // still usable and nothing else in it depends on either service.
+  AutocompleteClassifier* const classifier =
+      AutocompleteClassifierFactory::GetForProfile(GetProfile());
+  if (!classifier) {
+    return;
+  }
+
   AutocompleteMatch match;
-  AutocompleteClassifierFactory::GetForProfile(GetProfile())
-      ->Classify(params_.selection_text, false, false,
-                 metrics::OmniboxEventProto::INVALID_SPEC, &match, nullptr);
+  classifier->Classify(params_.selection_text, false, false,
+                       metrics::OmniboxEventProto::INVALID_SPEC, &match,
+                       nullptr);
   selection_navigation_url_ = match.destination_url;
   if (!selection_navigation_url_.is_valid()) {
     return;
@@ -2889,9 +2908,15 @@ void RenderViewContextMenu::AppendSearchProvider() {
   EscapeAmpersands(&printable_selection_text);
 
   if (AutocompleteMatch::IsSearchType(match.type)) {
+    // ATRIUM: same shape as the classifier above. The null RESULT
+    // was already handled; the null SERVICE was not.
+    TemplateURLService* const template_urls =
+        TemplateURLServiceFactory::GetForProfile(GetProfile());
+    if (!template_urls) {
+      return;
+    }
     const TemplateURL* const default_provider =
-        TemplateURLServiceFactory::GetForProfile(GetProfile())
-            ->GetDefaultSearchProvider();
+        template_urls->GetDefaultSearchProvider();
     if (!default_provider) {
       return;
     }
